WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:14,460
Typically, how long should I wait until I get another cheek swab test?

00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:23,220
Well, it depends on if it's your so so typically what after your initial cheek swab test I

00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:33,620
Typically recommend getting another one 30 60 or 90 days depending on how fast I think your protocol may change

00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,620
and

00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:39,700
How ill a person is we want to stay on top of things

00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,100
You know more rapidly

00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:53,580
So, but you know, I've had people where they do the initial cheek swab test and literally we it's like they've gone off the face of the earth

00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,580
We haven't heard for them in two years

00:00:56,180 --> 00:01:00,340
So I think as much as I don't want to create a

00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,780
patient base that is

00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,780
co-dependent on us I

00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:10,220
Also don't want people to think that they can't communicate with us

00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,500
So I think there's a balance between creating a co-dependent relationship and

00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:19,260
Not utilizing the services that you paid for

00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:26,340
So I feel sad what I haven't heard from people for a long long time in one sense

00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:31,540
Because I miss them. I hope they're doing well. I don't even know if they're doing well. I

00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:34,540
also understand that

00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:40,300
Some people are doing great and they don't want to do anything else. They feel great

00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:44,620
And they feel like they're going to handle on things and they got what they paid for I get that also

00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:50,060
So I'm trying to understand that balance wherever a person is at and accept that

00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,220
But typically I

00:01:53,220 --> 00:02:00,340
Think you should get retested, you know after your initial cheek swab test within about 60 to 90 days

00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:09,180
And then after that it depends on if things change so if your symptoms change if you're

00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:16,020
Objective findings change meaning your tests are getting worse. You're feeling worse that you should do it again

00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:21,740
If things are you're doing great and things are doing great and you're objective findings

00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:25,020
And say you're still with an oncologist and your CT scan is coming back

00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:30,420
No evidence of disease. I mean, I guess I would just stay in the course and stay doing what you're doing

00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,740
so

00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:39,660
You know, many times when we talked I think I spoke to a person recently haven't heard from for a couple years and he's doing great and

00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,500
Okay, well, that's fantastic

00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:49,500
But I also you want to encourage people to stay in communication with us

00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:53,980
For our sake, too

00:02:53,980 --> 00:03:01,300
So yeah, it depends on you know, I always said that you do another cheek swab kind of like if you you'd go to the doctor because something changed

00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:03,780
Something was new or you're trying to

00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:11,780
Objectify what is going on and making decisions on supplements and diet to things so you should stay atop of it

00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:18,300
But I also know that person is doing really well. They may just stay the course as long as they're doing really well

00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:20,300
So it's a balance there

